<title>SWITZERLAND: TENNIS-HINGIS HURT IN FALL FROM HORSE, NEWSPAPER SAYS.</title>
<headline>TENNIS-HINGIS HURT IN FALL FROM HORSE, NEWSPAPER SAYS.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>World number one Martina Hingis is expected to miss the next three tennis tournaments after injuring her knee in a fall from her horse, Blick newspaper said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>According to Blick, a Swiss-German tabloid, Hingis injured her leg on Monday while out riding and will be out of action for three weeks, missing tournaments in Hamburg, Rome and Berlin.</p>
<p>The paper said that surgery was not needed.</p>
